DevOps Interview Command Series — Nexus Repository (Day 8) 📦

Nexus is the artifact backbone of CI/CD pipelines.
From storing build outputs to promoting versions across environments, Nexus ensures controlled and secure artifact management.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Nexus commands & operations you must know:

systemctl start nexus
systemctl status nexus
systemctl restart nexus

tail -f /opt/sonatype/nexus/log/nexus.log

curl -u user:password http://nexus_url/service/rest/v1/repositories
curl -u user:password http://nexus_url/service/rest/v1/assets

mvn deploy
mvn deploy -DskipTests

npm publish --registry=http://nexus_url/repository/npm-hosted/
npm install pkg --registry=http://nexus_url/repository/npm-group/

docker login nexus_url
docker tag image:tag nexus_url/repo/image:tag
docker push nexus_url/repo/image:tag

curl -u user:password -X DELETE http://nexus_url/service/rest/v1/components/ID

🎯 Interview Focus
• Hosted vs Proxy vs Group repositories
• Artifact promotion & versioning strategy
• Securing repositories with roles & permissions
• Cleaning unused artifacts (cleanup policies)
• Integrating Nexus with CI/CD pipelines
